      "writtenOn": "2024-12-06T15:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s valid to do `memset(\u0026fragment, 0, sizeof(wgpu::FragmentState))` for dawn C++ structs since it would overwrite non-POD member data. For example, FragmentState::entryPoint is a wgpu::StringView. We can initialize this as `wgpu::FragmentState fragment \u003d {};` which follows aggregate initialization rules and will ensure all member variables are initialized, either with their default member initializer or zero initialized. That\u0027s probably the best solution here but I was copying the VertexState initialization that listed constantCount/constants explicitly.\n\n\u003e I think this should be fixed in Dawn if possible\n\nI can ask dawn team about this. It would be handy to not have to worry about.",
      "parentUuid": "31f8e5c5_7e5a34e1",
      "revId": "e922bd02f351ebd27ae58f02323d7a72ec47838a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
